---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Badge from '../components/Badge.astro';
import Heading from '../components/typography/Heading.astro';
import Body from '../components/typography/Body.astro';
---

<Layout title="Portfolio - Saad Shahd">
  <Container width="default">
    <Heading level={1} as="h1" class="mb-2">Portfolio</Heading>
    <Body size="lg" as="p" class="text-neutral mb-8">Selected case studies showcasing technical depth and impact</Body>

    <div class="grid gap-8 md:gap-16">
      <!-- Statsbomb Case Study -->
      <Card variant="case-study" href="/portfolio/statsbomb">
        <div class="p-8">
          <Heading level={3} as="h2" class="mb-4">Statsbomb Collection</Heading>
          <Body size="base" as="p" class="text-neutral mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            How do you scale real-time sports data collection without sacrificing correctness?
            Started with an Electron app (XState state machines, 30+ contextual keyboard shortcuts) that reduced 16 sequential hours to 4 concurrent collectors.
            Then built backend DSLs so product managers could define sports rules as configuration—new sports became data, not code.
            But architecture alone isn't enough: learning to build team ownership took until year three, and geo-political constraints meant the final piece—customer-facing DSLs—never shipped.
            Lessons: Architectural separation eliminates false trade-offs. Team building shapes what's sustainable. Context determines what works.
          </Body>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
            <Badge variant="category">Real-Time Collaboration</Badge>
            <Badge variant="status">Kafka</Badge>
            <Badge variant="status">XState</Badge>
            <Badge variant="skill">ANTLR</Badge>
          </div>
          <Body size="sm" as="div" class="text-neutral">
            Problem → Architecture → Impact → Lessons
          </Body>
        </div>
      </Card>

      <!-- Future Case Study Placeholder 1 -->
      <Card variant="case-study">
        <div class="p-8 opacity-50">
          <Heading level={3} as="h2" class="mb-4"><span>Wise Editorial Platform</span></Heading>
          <Body size="base" as="p" class="text-neutral mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            How do 20 teams collaborate on wise.com without friction or incorrectness?
            Building editorial infrastructure that handles global→local fintech complexity—regulations differ by market, offerings vary by country, cultural nuances matter.
            The challenge is architectural: coherence at scale while preserving developer experience.
            Still exploring what content collaboration looks like at 16M+ customer scale.
          </Body>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
            <Badge variant="skill">TypeScript</Badge>
            <Badge variant="skill">React</Badge>
            <Badge variant="skill">Content Architecture</Badge>
            <Badge variant="skill">DX</Badge>
          </div>
          <Body size="sm" as="div" class="text-neutral">
            Coming soon...
          </Body>
        </div>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
